From f5fce0c265c4d24df7b11620a2e03d2218a189c7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: nuubOS Project <noreply@nuubos.invalid>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 16:03:22 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] GLES: texture atlas in cached memory, a new texture per
 upload

YabaSanshiro decoded every texture of a frame into a mapped pixel unpack
buffer and uploaded the atlas from it twice a frame (after the VDP1 and
the VDP2 commands) into the same texture. On the H700 GPU buffers are
mapped write-combined and Panfrost copies a PBO upload with the CPU, so
each upload read the whole atlas back from uncached memory, and it had
to wait for the GPU to finish drawing with the texture first
(DRM_PANFROST_WAIT_BO).

The atlas is now ordinary memory uploaded with glTexSubImage2D, and each
upload goes to the next of four textures (two uploads a frame, two frames
in flight). Virtua Fighter 2 fight (RG CubeXX): 18.5 -> 27.5 fps; the
memcpy went from 28 % to 5 % of the emulation thread, the wait from 7 %
to under 1 %.

Upstream-Status: Pending
